,"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids July to August came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years. In 2025 that middle ran 24% of normal in August to September and 32% in September to October. In 2026 so far it swung the other way, with April to May at 171% and May to June at 171%. Grid 11227 had its driest year in 2022 at 43% of normal.</p>"}
